Launch an EC2 Instance and Connect

========================================================
========================================================
========================================================
PART A — Launch Linux EC2 Instance
========================================================

Step 1:
Login to AWS Console / AWS Academy Learner Lab.

Step 2:
Choose Region:
• Asia Pacific (Mumbai)
OR
• N. Virginia

Step 3:
Go to:
Services → EC2 → Launch Instance

Step 4:
Configure Instance:
1. Name: My_VS1
2. AMI: Ubuntu / Amazon Linux
3. Architecture: Default 64-bit (x86)
4. Instance Type: t3.micro
5. Create New Key Pair
• Type: RSA
• Format: .pem
6. Keep default network/storage settings
7. Click Launch Instance

========================================================
PART B — Connect Using SSH
========================================================

Step 1:
Open Terminal / PowerShell / Git Bash

Step 2:
Go to key location:

cd Downloads

Step 3:
Give permission to key:

chmod 400 mykey.pem

Step 4:
Connect to Ubuntu EC2:

ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@<Public-IP>

For Amazon Linux:

ssh -i mykey.pem ec2-user@<Public-IP>

Step 5:
Connected Successfully

========================================================
PART C — Connect Using PuTTY
========================================================

Step 1:
Install PuTTY and PuTTYgen

Step 2:
Convert .pem to .ppk
1. Open PuTTYgen
2. Click Load
3. Select .pem file
4. Click Save Private Key
5. Save as keyname.ppk

Step 3:
Open PuTTY

Host Name:

ubuntu@<Public-IP>

OR

ec2-user@<Public-IP>

Step 4:
Attach .ppk Key
Go to:

Connection → SSH → Auth → Credentials

Browse and select .ppk file

Step 5:
Click Open

Connected Successfully

========================================================
PART D — Connect Using AWS CloudShell
========================================================

Step 1:
Open CloudShell in AWS Console

Step 2:
Upload .pem file

Step 3:
Run:

chmod 400 mykey.pem

Step 4:
Connect:

ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@<Public-IP>

OR

ssh -i mykey.pem ec2-user@<Public-IP>

Connected Successfully

========================================================
PART E — Launch Windows EC2 and Connect Using RDP
========================================================

Step 1:
Launch Windows EC2 Instance
• Select Windows Server AMI
• Instance Type: t2.micro
• Allow RDP Port 3389
• Download .pem key

Step 2:
Get Administrator Password
EC2 → Connect → RDP Client → Get Password

Upload .pem file and decrypt password

Step 3:
Open Remote Desktop

mstsc

Step 4:
Enter Public IP / DNS

Login:
Username: Administrator
Password: Decrypted Password

Connected Successfully

