AWS BASTION HOST + PRIVATE DATABASE SETUP (COMPLETE GUIDE)

========================================================
========================================================

VPC CONFIGURATION
========================================================
VPC:
Name: myvpc
CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16

Subnets:
Public Subnet (Bastion):

Name: PublicSubnet
CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24
Private Subnet (DB):

Name: PrivateSubnet
CIDR: 10.0.2.0/24
========================================================
2. INTERNET GATEWAY
Create Internet Gateway
Attach to myvpc
========================================================
3. ROUTE TABLES
Public Route Table:

Destination: 0.0.0.0/0 → Internet Gateway
Associate: PublicSubnet
Private Route Table:

Destination: 10.0.0.0/16 → local
Associate: PrivateSubnet
========================================================
4. SECURITY GROUPS

A) BASTION SECURITY GROUP
Inbound Rules:

SSH | Port 22 | Source: My IP
Outbound Rules:

All traffic | 0.0.0.0/0

B) DATABASE SECURITY GROUP
Inbound Rules:

SSH | Port 22 | Source: 10.0.1.0/24 (Bastion subnet)
MYSQL/Aurora | Port 3306 | Source: 10.0.2.0/24
Outbound Rules:

All traffic | 0.0.0.0/0
========================================================
5. EC2 INSTANCE CONFIGURATION

BASTION INSTANCE
Subnet: PublicSubnet
Auto-assign Public IP: Enabled
Security Group: Bastion SG
Key Pair: bastion.pem

DATABASE INSTANCE
Subnet: PrivateSubnet
Auto-assign Public IP: Disabled
Security Group: DB SG
Key Pair: ebs_test_key.pem
========================================================
6. CONNECTIVITY FLOW
Windows PC
↓ SSH
Bastion Host (Public Subnet)
↓ SSH (Private IP)
Database Server (Private Subnet)

========================================================
7. CONNECTION COMMANDS

Step 1: Connect to Bastion
ssh -i bastion.pem ubuntu@<BASTION_PUBLIC_IP>


Step 2: Copy DB Key to Bastion
scp -i bastion.pem ebs_test_key.pem ubuntu@<BASTION_PUBLIC_IP>:/home/ubuntu/


Step 3: Fix Permissions in Bastion
chmod 400 ebs_test_key.pem


Step 4: Connect to DB Server
ssh -i ebs_test_key.pem ec2-user@10.0.2.26

========================================================
8. DATABASE ADMINISTRATION TASKS

Install MySQL
sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install mysql-server -y

(or Ubuntu)
sudo apt update
sudo apt install mysql-server -y


Start MySQL Service
sudo systemctl start mysqld


Check Status
sudo systemctl status mysqld


Enable at Boot
sudo systemctl enable mysqld


Restart MySQL
sudo systemctl restart mysqld

