========================================================
AWS NORMAL VPC SETUP (BASIC EC2 DEPLOYMENT)

========================================================

VPC CREATION
========================================================
VPC:
Name: NormalVPC
CIDR Block: 10.0.0.0/16
This VPC is used for a simple public EC2 setup (no Bastion, no private subnet).

========================================================
2. SUBNET CREATION
Public Subnet:

Name: PublicSubnet
CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24
Availability Zone: any (same region)
========================================================
3. INTERNET GATEWAY
Create Internet Gateway
Attach to NormalVPC
========================================================
4. ROUTE TABLE
Public Route Table:

Destination: 0.0.0.0/0 → Internet Gateway
Associate with PublicSubnet
========================================================
5. SECURITY GROUP
Security Group Name: WebSG

Inbound Rules:

SSH | Port 22 | Source: My IP
HTTP | Port 80 | Source: 0.0.0.0/0 (optional for web server)
HTTPS | Port 443 | Source: 0.0.0.0/0 (optional)
Outbound Rules:

All traffic | 0.0.0.0/0
========================================================
6. EC2 INSTANCE SETUP
Instance:

Name: Public-EC2
AMI: Amazon Linux 2023
Instance Type: t3.micro
Key Pair: normal-key.pem (or any created key)
Network Settings:

VPC: NormalVPC
Subnet: PublicSubnet
Auto-assign Public IP: Enabled
Security Group: WebSG
========================================================
7. CONNECT TO INSTANCE
From Windows:

ssh -i "normal-key.pem" ec2-user@<PUBLIC_IP>

========================================================
8. OPTIONAL WEB SERVER SETUP
Install Apache:

sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install httpd -y
sudo systemctl start httpd
sudo systemctl enable httpd

Test:

Open browser → http://<PUBLIC_IP>
========================================================
9. FINAL ARCHITECTURE
Internet
↓
Internet Gateway
↓
Public Subnet (10.0.1.0/24)
↓
EC2 Instance (Public IP enabled)

